==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Acarodermatitis Hand.jpg|thumb|scabies of the hand]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|scabies}}, {{m|enm|scabiez}}, from {{der|en|la|scabiēs|t=scurf; scab, mange, itch}}, from {{m|la|scabō|t=scratch, scrape|pos=verb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈskeɪ.biz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-scabies.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪbiz}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪbiːz|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} An infestation of parasitic [[mite]]s, ''[[Sarcoptes scabiei]]'', causing intense itching caused by the mites burrowing into the skin of humans and other animals. It is easily transmissible from human to human; secondary skin infection may occur.
#: {{syn|en|leprosy|q1=obsolete}}
#: {{cot|en|mange|q1=in animals}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1889|title=The Advance of Science in the Last Half-Century|author=[[w:Thomas Henry Huxley|T. H. Huxley]]|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/15253/15253-h/15253-h.htm|passage=Further, just as the discovery of the cause of '''scabies''' proved the absurdity of many of the old prescriptions for the prevention and treatment of that disease; so the discovery of the cause of splenic fever, and other such maladies, has given a new direction to prophylactic and curative measures against the worst scourges of humanity.}}

